      "message": "[error] Line 188: 🔴 The UUID prevents stale callbacks from resolving a retry, but this now permits multiple live Telecom requests for the same `Call`: every later RINGING/media update can create another `PendingIncomingCall` and call `addNewIncomingCall` even while a SHOW_UI request remains resolved in this map. Both connections bind to the same native call, while `Call.systemConnection` retains only the first, producing duplicate Telecom UI and an un-routed connection retained until termination. Reuse an existing live request for the call (or explicitly supersede and dispose it) while keeping per-generation keys for late callbacks.",
