      "message": "[error] Line 851: 🔴 This still collapses a hosted/swarm conference when `conferenceChanged` is delivered before `conferenceCreated`: the `getOrPut` conference has both `conversationId \u003d\u003d null` and `hostCall \u003d\u003d null`, so the one-participant update satisfies `canCollapseToSimpleCall`, removes the conference, and detaches the last call before the creation event can restore its metadata. The later creation then builds a new conference and loses the original hosted identity/host binding. Defer this collapse until creation metadata is known, or preserve an explicit hosted/pending marker from the update path; add a regression test for changed-before-created ordering.",
